                "entry_id": "c2c65be9-4dfe-3dfe-9384-ff176b5cb2d0",
                "word": "érismature",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "8e2e1f6b-d1e1-45ec-bacf-41ccf399363f",
                        "entry_id": "c2c65be9-4dfe-3dfe-9384-ff176b5cb2d0",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "érismatures"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "103bd00b-3777-34b5-ae35-5e44c3e8e4bd",
                        "entry_id": "c2c65be9-4dfe-3dfe-9384-ff176b5cb2d0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Nom vernaculaire de certaines espèces d’oiseaux palmipèdes de la famille des anatidés, canards de surface."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "759d4caa-c9e1-4c17-ac6e-57a9c740185c",
                                "sense_id": "103bd00b-3777-34b5-ae35-5e44c3e8e4bd",
                                "text": "Les œufs de l’Érismature couronnée et, autant que nous avons pu en juger, ceux des autres espèces du genre, présentent un […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "48ee714e-1d71-428a-8f38-c36a93cbbad0",
                                "sense_id": "103bd00b-3777-34b5-ae35-5e44c3e8e4bd",
                                "text": "Enfin l’Érismature couronné, le Harle vulgaire, le Bièvre huppé et la Piette ou petit Harle huppé."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d1674006-956a-4f6a-b188-4f5dbc5bc1a0",
                                "sense_id": "103bd00b-3777-34b5-ae35-5e44c3e8e4bd",
                                "text": "Les érismatures roux ne sont habituellement pas présents en Europe ; ceux qui s’y trouvent sont […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "06929ea3-a044-42c1-8f2d-98db8a6c413c",
                                "sense_id": "103bd00b-3777-34b5-ae35-5e44c3e8e4bd",
                                "text": "Des dispositions identiques risquent d’être maintenant adoptées par les décideurs français contre l’érismature rousse, un canard importé des États-Unis, qui s’accouple avec l’érismature à tête blanche d’Europe."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "30dfb330-2b73-4621-b8ba-d547d695b510",
                                "sense_id": "103bd00b-3777-34b5-ae35-5e44c3e8e4bd",
                                "text": "La Liste des oiseaux de la contrée d’Astrakhan établie par le père de Khlebnikov mentionne 341 espèces différentes. Cormoran, pélican, aigrette rouge, bihoreau, spatule blanche, érismature, macreuse, tadorne, butor, crécerelle, gerfaut, busard, guêpier, faucon, hobereau, faucon pèlerin, laneret, étourneau, chevêche, huppe, grand-duc, ganfa-syrhapte, tourterelle, oedicnème, bécassine, bécasse, épervier."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bb25a1d5-4555-4ce4-a5ec-532821ea529f",
                        "source_entry_id": "c2c65be9-4dfe-3dfe-9384-ff176b5cb2d0",
                        "source_sense_id": "103bd00b-3777-34b5-ae35-5e44c3e8e4bd",
                        "target_lang_word": "ruddy duck",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ruddy duck",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bc9bb8fc-03ab-372a-8275-7f65aea805aa",
                                        "entry_id": "6fd37725-e010-3f89-8714-fe3577a4dca9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Oxyura jamaicensis, a small stifftail duck, the male of which has a rust-coloured body."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6b3d337-abcf-4b04-b001-6945609e0f84",
                                                "sense_id": "bc9bb8fc-03ab-372a-8275-7f65aea805aa",
                                                "text": "Except when migrating, the ruddy duck seldom flies.[…]If disturbed by a predator, the ruddy duck dives to escape."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66a21f71-7b68-433c-a2ae-30e36b1f35f0",
                                                "sense_id": "bc9bb8fc-03ab-372a-8275-7f65aea805aa",
                                                "text": "Since hybridization with the ruddy duck could lead to extinction of the white-headed duck, Spain began to kill its ruddy ducks. Trials to eliminate ruddy ducks from the U.K. began in 1999, and were overseen by a euphemistically named White-headed Duck Task Force."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "500588d6-127e-4169-923a-12deefb8ab1e",
                                                "sense_id": "bc9bb8fc-03ab-372a-8275-7f65aea805aa",
                                                "text": "The decision was taken, supported by conservation organizations, that it was necessary to save the white-headed duck species by exterminating all members of the ruddy duck species in Europe, which meant mainly in the UK, where there were an estimated 6000 ruddy ducks in 2000."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
